cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference this proof, paper, or formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "A proof of the Aaronson–Ambainis conjecture, with a Lean 4 formalization"
version: 1.1.0
authors:
  - family-names: "Turturean"
    given-names: "David"
    affiliation: "PSI"
    email: "david@psi.inc"
date-released: 2026-11-06
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/physical-superintelligence/aaronson-ambainis"
abstract: >-
  A bounded polynomial of degree at most d on the discrete cube with variance
  at least epsilon has a variable of influence at least (epsilon/d)^7, as
  conjectured by Aaronson and Ambainis. This repository contains the paper
  and a Lean 4 formalization against Mathlib v4.33.0 whose final statement
  uses only Mathlib definitions.
keywords:
  - "Aaronson–Ambainis conjecture"
  - "influence"
  - "bounded polynomials"
  - "Boolean functions"
  - "fractional block sensitivity"
  - "quantum query complexity"
  - "Lean 4"
  - "formal verification"
